ileges within the container","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a container privilege escalation flaw was found in certain multi-cloud object gateway core images. this issue stems from the /etc/passwd file being created with group-writable permissions during build time. in certain conditions, an attacker who can execute commands within an affected container, even as a non-root user, can leverage their membership in the root group to modify the /etc/passwd file. this could allow the attacker to add a new user with any arbitrary uid, including uid 0, leading to full root privileges within the container"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Openshift Data Foundation 4.22","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift data foundation 4.22"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-276","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-276"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-33814","predicate":"adp-affects-cpe","object":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10.2","source":"vulnrichment","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10.2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-33814","predicate":"adp-affects-cpe","object":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux_eus:10.0","source":"vulnrichment","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux_eus:10.0"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-33814","predicate":"adp-affects-cpe","object":"cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:8","source":"vulnrichment","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_